+## Native threading: separate untuned and PGO-tuned evidence
+
+Use **no runtime PGO and no manual hierarchy cost overrides** as the primary
+comparison when assessing the progress-protocol/padding prototype. Keep
+Verilator's automatically generated static child costs: these are ordinary
+hierarchical generation, not runtime training. For 5.052 the generated 47,230
+child cost already dominated the earlier manual 10,000 hint (hierarchical costs
+combine by maximum); removing the custom file therefore did not itself change
+that estimate.
+
+The September 23 M5 Max / Apple Clang 21 / Verilator 5.052 experiment holds
+physical 16×8, Proc+Endpoint, blocking caches, iPoly on, inputs and native
+compiler settings fixed. Five-worker counter/progress models have identical
+task bodies and lane order; only the synchronization implementation differs.
+Whole-process wall means are:
+
+| Workload | One worker | Five: counters | Five: progress + padding | Progress speedup vs one | Progress wall reduction vs counters |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| PageRank wiki-Vote/pod36 | 25.860 s | 23.423 s | 23.130 s | 1.118× | 1.25% |
+| AES NUM-ITER_2 | 75.140 s | 67.220 s | 66.050 s | 1.138× | 1.74% |
+
+These are three PageRank and two AES trials/mode, not a general scaling claim.
+The primary sequences have no display transition. An initial AES sequence was
+preserved but excluded in full after its power log revealed display sleep
+during a trial; the same six positions were repeated under `caffeinate -diu`.
+All 24 executions (primary, warmup and excluded original AES) passed and
+reproduced all 128 ordered marker pairs exactly. Kernel envelopes remain
+14,497/388,176 cycles. Five progress workers use about 3.92×/3.86× aggregate
+CPU-seconds for these modest latency gains, not evidence of energy savings.
+
+The separately collected September 22 **PGO-tuned** 5.052 series measured
+3.64%/3.66% incremental wall reduction and 1.252×/1.290× overall speedup. Report
+those as conditional on the tuned schedule, not ordinary untuned operation.
+The untuned and tuned models have the same task bodies but different schedules;
+cross-day host conditions also differ, so this is not an interleaved causal
+PGO-on/off test. Do not import the older 5.050 speedups into either comparison.
+
+The [compact evidence](evidence/native-untuned-5052-2026-09-23.json) pins both
+datasets, source/tool/model identities, trial values, environmental exclusions
+and raw paths. Core placement/frequency and continuous background activity were
+not controlled. The prototype combines protocol and padding rather than
+isolating each. No shared default changed; these bounded results do not justify
+replacing the one-worker default.
+
+Reusable lesson: hold display state as well as system sleep stable for
+percent-level macOS timing comparisons, record environmental exclusions before
+repeating the complete affected block, and preserve every original sample.
+
